# The influence functions of particle mesh Ewald on the host
# (lib/Driver/Influence.cpp, D[p3m-influence]) against sums over the aliases
# written out in the test (test/Driver/InfluenceTest.cpp):
#
# - influence "OPTIMAL" is eq. 4.2 of Ballenegger et al. (2012) per edge, to
#   the truncation of its sums at |j| <= 50 (3e-7 at order 4, rounding at
#   order 8), and within 3.3e-6 of eq. 4.2 with the sums at |j| <= 2;
# - eq. 4.1 (influence "P3M") in a rectangular cell, as the kernels compute
#   it from the rows of the edges, is the direct sum over the aliases
#   max_a |J_a| <= 2 to rounding, and so are the sums its virial takes;
# - the virial of a point is -dE/de of the direct sum under each of the nine
#   strains of the cell, to 1e-9 of the energy of the point;
# - the truncation at |j| <= 2 changes eq. 4.1 by at most 5e-5 of it at
#   order 4 (against |j| <= 12), where it is above 1e-6 of its largest value.
#
# RUN: mdir-influence-test | FileCheck %s
# CHECK-NOT: FAIL
# CHECK: K 64 order 4: max |OPTIMAL / eq. 4.2 - 1|, |j| <= 50: {{.*}} ok
# CHECK: 64x64x64 order 4 beta 0.3947: eq. 4.1, edges against the direct sum: {{.*}} ok
# CHECK: 64x64x64 order 4: virial against -dE/de: {{.*}} ok
# CHECK: 20x18x16 order 8: max |G(|j|<=2) / G(|j|<=12) - 1| {{.*}} ok
# CHECK: 0 failures
